course: dictionary
lesson: 13704
title: When words and feelings do not match
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Insincerity means saying or showing feelings you do not really have. A person who is insincere is not being honest about what they feel. Their words or actions say one thing, but their true feelings are different.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Mia said, "What a lovely present!" but she rolled her eyes as soon as Ben turned away.» Her words say she loves the present, but her eyes show she does not. That gap between words and feelings is insincerity.
explain: Context helps again. «The headteacher's praise sounded fake, and his smile never reached his eyes.» Fake and never reaching his eyes are clues that his words are not true to how he feels. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "The headteacher was not honest about how he felt" still makes sense.
fact: Insincerity is a noun. You can show insincerity, or notice it in someone.
fact: Insincerity means saying or showing feelings you do not really have.
fact: A sincere person is honest about what they truly feel.
fact: Insincerity is an uncountable noun, so it does not usually have a plural form.
fact: Writers use insincerity to show the reader that a character's words do not match their true feelings.
exercise: «Her congratulations were full of insincerity; she did not mean a word.» What does insincerity mean? | Shouting loudly when you are happy | *Saying or showing feelings you do not really have | Feeling sleepy after a long day | Being very honest about your feelings
exercise: Which word means the opposite of insincerity, being honest about your true feelings? | *sincerity | boredom | rudeness | surprise
exercise: «The boy said sorry, but he was grinning from ear to ear.» What does the grin suggest? | That he has lost his bag | That he is feeling cold | *That his words do not match his true feelings | That he is very sorry and upset
test: «Tom said, "I love your drawing!" while he gave a big, bored yawn.» What does the yawn show? | That Tom is tired and truly loves the drawing | *That Tom's praise is insincere | That Tom has a cold | That Tom is about to sing
test: Which is the best example of insincerity? | *Ana said, "I love these socks!" while she hid them secretly under her bed | Ana said, "Thanks for the hat!" and gave her friend a warm hug | Ana laughed at the joke and clapped her hands | Ana cried when she read the sad letter
exam: Read: «The mayor's speech was full of insincerity, and nobody believed a word he said.» What does this tell us? | The mayor was truly honest and sincere | The mayor was very tired after the speech | *The mayor's words did not match his true feelings | The speech was all about the weather
